  "files": [
    {
      "path": "index.html",
      "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>Pixel Temperature Converter</title>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"styles.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class=\"card\">\n    <h1>Temperature Converter</h1>\n    <form id=\"converter-form\">\n      <div class=\"field\">\n        <label for=\"temperature\">Temperature</label>\n        <input type=\"text\" id=\"temperature\" name=\"temperature\" placeholder=\"e.g. 100\" autocomplete=\"off\">\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"field\">\n        <label for=\"direction\">Direction</label>\n        <select id=\"direction\" name=\"direction\">\n          <option value=\"c-to-f\">Celsius to Fahrenheit</option>\n          <option value=\"f-to-c\">Fahrenheit to Celsius</option>\n        </select>\n      </div>\n      <button type=\"button\" id=\"convert\">Convert</button>\n    </form>\n    <p class=\"output\" id=\"result\">--</p>\n    <div class=\"formulas\">\n      <p>C to F: x * 9/5 + 32</p>\n      <p>F to C: (x - 32) * 5/9</p>\n    </div>\n  </main>\n  <script src=\"script.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "description": ""
    },
    {
      "path": "styles.css",
      "content": "* {\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n}\n\nbody {\n  min-height: 100vh;\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  background: #1e1e2f;\n  background-image: linear-gradient(45deg, #2a2a40 25%, transparent 25%),\n                    linear-gradient(-45deg, #2a2a40 25%, transparent 25%),\n                    linear-gradient(45deg, transparent 75%, #2a2a40 75%),\n                    linear-gradient(-45deg, transparent 75%, #2a2a40 75%);\n  background-size: 16px 16px;\n  font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace;\n  font-size: 16px;\n  color: #f0f0f0;\n  padding: 16px;\n}\n\n.card {\n  background: #2a2a40;\n  border: 4px solid #f0f0f0;\n  border-radius: 0;\n  padding: 24px;\n  width: 100%;\n  max-width: 400px;\n  box-shadow: 8px 8px 0 #0f0f1a;\n}\n\nh1 {\n  font-size: 1.5rem;\n  text-align: center;\n  margin-bottom: 24px;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 2px;\n  color: #ffd700;\n}\n\n.field {\n  margin-bottom: 16px;\n}\n\nlabel {\n  display: block;\n  margin-bottom: 8px;\n  font-weight: bold;\n  color: #a0d0ff;\n}\n\ninput, select, button {\n  width: 100%;\n  padding: 12px;\n  font-family: inherit;\n  font-size: 1rem;\n  background: #1e1e2f;\n  color: #f0f0f0;\n  border: 3px solid #a0d0ff;\n  border-radius: 0;\n  outline: none;\n  transition: border-color 0.1s, background 0.1s;\n}\n\ninput:focus, select:focus, button:focus {\n  border-color: #ffd700;\n  background: #2a2a40;\n}\n\nbutton {\n  background: #a0d0ff;\n  color: #1e1e2f;\n  font-weight: bold;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 1px;\n  margin-top: 8px;\n}\n\nbutton:hover {\n  background: #ffd700;\n  border-color: #ffd700;\n}\n\nbutton:active {\n  transform: translate(2px, 2px);\n  box-shadow: none;\n}\n\n.output {\n  font-size: 1.5rem;\n  text-align: center;\n  margin: 24px 0;\n  padding: 12px;\n  background: #1e1e2f;\n  border: 3px dashed #a0d0ff;\n  color: #ffd700;\n  font-weight: bold;\n}\n\n.formulas {\n  font-size: 0.9rem;\n  color: #a0d0ff;\n  text-align: center;\n  border-top: 2px solid #a0d0ff;\n  padding-top: 16px;\n}\n\n.formulas p {\n  margin: 4px 0;\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 360px) {\n  .card {\n    padding: 16px;\n  }\n  h1 {\n    font-size: 1.2rem;\n  }\n}",
      "description": ""
    },
    {
      "path": "script.js",
      "content": "document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {\n  const temperatureInput = document.getElementById('temperature');\n  const directionSelect = document.getElementById('direction');\n  const convertButton = document.getElementById('convert');\n  const resultOutput = document.getElementById('result');\n\n  function convert() {\n    const rawValue = temperatureInput.value.trim();\n    const direction = directionSelect.value;\n\n    if (rawValue === '') {\n      resultOutput.textContent = 'Error';\n      return;\n    }\n\n    const value = Number(rawValue);\n\n    if (!Number.isFinite(value)) {\n      resultOutput.textContent = 'Error';\n      return;\n    }\n\n    let converted;\n    if (direction === 'c-to-f') {\n      converted = value * 9 / 5 + 32;\n    } else if (direction === 'f-to-c') {\n      converted = (value - 32) * 5 / 9;\n    } else {\n      resultOutput.textContent = 'Error';\n      return;\n    }\n\n    resultOutput.textContent = converted.toFixed(2);\n  }\n\n  convertButton.addEventListener('click', convert);\n});",
      "description": ""
    },
    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel Temperature Converter\n\nA retro pixel-style temperature converter built with plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Works fully offline.\n\n## Features\n\n- Convert Celsius to Fahrenheit and Fahrenheit to Celsius\n- Pixel-art inspired UI with a cohesive 4-color palette\n- Keyboard-accessible controls with visible focus states\n- Responsive layout down to 360px width\n- Input validation: empty or non-finite input shows \"Error\"\n- Output formatted to exactly two decimal places (no units)\n\n## Formulas\n\n- **Celsius to Fahrenheit:** `x * 9/5 + 32`\n- **Fahrenheit to Celsius:** `(x - 32) * 5/9`\n\n## Usage\n\n1. Open `index.html` in any modern browser.\n2. Enter a numeric temperature in the input field.\n3. Select the conversion direction from the dropdown.\n4. Click the **Convert** button.\n5. The result appears below, formatted to two decimals.\n\n## Error Handling\n\n- Empty input or non-numeric/non-finite values display exactly `Error`.\n\n## File Structure\n\n- `index.html` — markup and labels\n- `styles.css` — pixel-themed styling\n- `script.js` — conversion logic and event listeners\n- `README.md` — this file\n\n## Constraints\n\n- No external dependencies, packages, or network requests.\n- No storage or server code.\n- Under 200 lines total.\n- Uses `addEventListener` (no inline handlers).\n",
      "description": ""
    }
  ]
